 when a base lane was `blocked` or `failed`, or a family a published baseline records as `uninspected`, hides it, and is excluded from `would_block` and the gate; `pre-existing` and `regressed` are unaffected), with the `unknown` ≤ 10 % rule counting PR runs that are `comparison: none` or carry such an `unknown` (§7.2, §7.3, A2). Phase 3 adds a `ruff` ignore. Phase 4's scenario reports area-ID retention (not X2's matched-area survival) and the Jaccard distribution; X2's thresholds are not a Phase 4 pass criterion. (5) The reusable workflow is two files split by trust level, `scout-guardian.yml` and `scout-guardian-trusted.yml` (§§7.4, 10.2, 11), and the pinned scanners are provisioned from the release tag, not the PR checkout (§7.4 CI toolchain provisioning, `404f69b`; REQ-25). (6) Statements made false by shipped Phase 1–4 facts are corrected (§§3.3, 4, 10.2, header). Appendix decisions of 2026-10-19 and 2026-10-22 other than 15 are unchanged.
 
